---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Start a comment thread, at a corner or on an object.
It prints the new thread with its thread id.

USAGE
  holst comment add <board> <text> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board
  text    The comment

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --at x,y          The corner of the thread in board units; a free corner by default
      --object object   The object the thread sits on: id, link or the first 8 characters of its id; not with --at
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst comment add "Roadmap" "Is Q3 final?" --object a1b2c3d4
  $ holst comment add "Roadmap" "Move this left" --at 120,80

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
